TITLE:: REReplay
summary:: A soundfile cued for replay into a NodeProxy or a Bus
categories:: Libraries>reCording
related:: Guides/reCording, Classes/RERecorder, Classes/RETake

DESCRIPTION::
Replays a take, typically into an output chain's signal for an AmbiX conversion, or into a bus. code::prepare:: (server running) cues the file with link::Classes/Buffer#*cueSoundFile:: and, for a proxy target, primes a link::Classes/DiskIn:: source into it (fade time 0, code::awake:: false: nothing plays until code::start::). code::free:: gives the proxy its fade time and code::awake:: back.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: server
argument:: path
argument:: numChannels
argument:: clock
argument:: ampDb
argument:: bufferSize
argument:: process
A code::{ |sig| }:: applied to the DiskIn output (a re-encoding, a gain).

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: into
argument:: proxyOrBus
A link::Classes/NodeProxy:: (the source is primed into it) or a link::Classes/Bus:: / index (a synth plays into it).
argument:: group
The group of the synth for a bus target. Chainable.
METHOD:: targetKind
code::\proxy::, code::\bus:: or nil.
METHOD:: prepare
METHOD:: start
argument:: quant
argument:: clock
argument:: amp
METHOD:: stop
METHOD:: set
argument:: key
argument:: value
The source's controls: code::\amp::.
